Traffic controls (data/controls.*, tools/controls/): besides OpenStreetMap, two authoritative datasets are merged in
(snapshots in data/controls-src/, pinned in tools/controls/sources.lock.json):
  - San Francisco Municipal Transportation Agency (SFMTA) traffic signals and stop signs, published on DataSF
    (datasets ybh5-27n2 and 4542-gpa3) under the Open Data Commons Public Domain Dedication and License (PDDL) 1.0.
  - City of San Jose, "City Owned Traffic Signals" (data.sanjoseca.gov), licensed under Creative Commons
    Attribution (CC BY; the portal lists http://www.opendefinition.org/licenses/cc-by). Attribution: "Contains data
    from the City of San Jose open data portal, licensed under CC BY." Changes: points snapped to the road graph, converted to per-approach controls.
Other city datasets listed in tools/controls/sources.json (Oakland, South San Francisco, Emeryville, Mountain View,
Cupertino) state no licence; they are used only for comparison and are not redistributed.
